<title>USA: Standard Missile wins $110 mln contract increase.</title>
<headline>Standard Missile wins $110 mln contract increase.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Navy said Friday it has awarded Standard Missile Co of McLean, Va., a $110 million increase to its contract to build 97 anti-aircraft and anti-ship Standard missiles for U.S. ships.</p>
<p>It said 41 percent of the work will be done at Bristol, Tenn.; 27 percent at Tucson, Ariz.; 17 percent at San Jose, Calif. and the rest at McLean, Irvine, Calif., and Chattanooga, Tenn.</p>
</text>
